cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ExoNotes: do ExoFOP follow-up comments carry disposition signal beyond the numeric catalogue?"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it, and cite the ExoFOP and NASA Exoplanet Archive sources it depends on."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ExoNotes contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE_ME/ExoNotes"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - TESS
  - ExoFOP
  - text-mining
  - calibration
  - negative-results
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered test of whether the free-text Comments astronomers write on TESS Objects of
  Interest contain disposition-relevant information not already present in the numeric catalogue
  columns. Free text is converted to numeric semantic features with a System One model (Jev,
  TypeSafe AI) used strictly as a featurizer; gradient boosting is the predictor and grouped
  cross-validation by host star is the arbiter. The study is designed so that a null result is
  publishable, and documents a measured label-echo rate of 47.9% in the ExoFOP comment corpus.
